  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Tai Bai Yun Sheng calls Immortal Crane Sect one of the ten great ancient sects of central continent, a force that surpasses Northern Plains super tribes.",
      "chapters": [
        654
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "immortal-crane-among-the-ten",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_tai_bai_yun_sheng",
        "fac_immortal_crane_sect",
        "reg_northern_plains"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan treats Immortal Crane Sect’s depth the same way: one of the ten great ancient sects, standing at Fei He mountain for hundreds of thousands of years. Narration adds that new sects keep rising in Central Continent and press those ten, who hold the region’s best cultivation resources and the most important positions.",
      "chapters": [
        658
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "immortal-crane-among-the-ten",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "loc_fei_he_mountain",
        "reg_central_continent"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The ten great ancient sects of central continent spend countless years arranging for progress inside Eighty-Eight True Yang Building. When Imperial Court blessed land is destroyed and the building collapses, that news is a huge nightmare for those sects after their long planning. Feng Jiu Ge also recalls that Fang Yuan snatched Hu Immortal blessed land under the eyes of all ten great ancient sects, while Immortal Crane Sect claimed him as one of their own and blocked the others from moving.",
      "chapters": [
        696
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "plot-on-true-yang-building",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_eighty_eight_true_yang_building",
        "loc_imperial_court_blessed_land",
        "char_feng_jiu_ge",
        "loc_hu_immortal_blessed_land"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Qin Bai Sheng recognizes Feng Jiu Ge as the number one person of Central Continent’s ten great ancient sects.",
      "chapters": [
        766
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "feng-jiu-ges-standing",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_qin_bai_sheng"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Black Heaven Temple is called one of the ten great ancient sects when Central Continent Gu Immortals argue reputation while hunting in Northern Plains. Bu Fei Yan represents Heavenly Lotus Sect of the ten great ancient sects in the same stretch.",
      "chapters": [
        811
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "named-member-sects",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_black_heaven_temple",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "char_bu_fei_yan",
        "fac_heavenly_lotus_sect"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Wind Cloud Manor is likewise named as one of the ten when Hong Chi Ming’s Gu formation background is explained.",
      "chapters": [
        923
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "named-member-sects",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_wind_cloud_manor",
        "char_hong_chi_ming",
        "sys_gu_formation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Combat Immortal Sect states the same membership when explaining its disciple selection rules.",
      "chapters": [
        1227
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "named-member-sects",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_combat_immortal_sect"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Central Continent’s Refinement Path Convention is created by the ten great ancient sects, with Heavenly Court supporting it in secret. Sign-up sites number in the hundreds across Central Continent, mostly sects closely linked to those ten or acting as their representatives, and the convention favors Central Continent Gu Masters and sects.",
      "chapters": [
        829
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "refinement-path-convention",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_refinement_path_convention",
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Central Continent’s ten great ancient sects are stronger than Southern Border in that comparison, and they share the same superior, Heavenly Court. They fight each other, yet unite like one body when foreign enemies appear.",
      "chapters": [
        2138
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "heavenly-court-superior",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_southern_border"
      ]
    }
  ],
